//? Title: Karn's ambiguity rule and the actual timeout state
//? Subtitle: Educational RTT smoothing, ignored ACKs and atomic checked backoff
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An ACK after retransmission may not identify which transmission it acknowledges.
Karn's rule avoids using that ambiguous RTT sample. This report inspects actual
estimator transitions, retains the original nine-event sequence, and
distinguishes an educational smoother from a complete TCP timer. Timeout
backoff, ignored samples, clean recovery and numerical failures are explicit;
native before/after snapshots come from the producing state transition.
)

\toc

> Ignore an ambiguous sample without undoing backoff

Initialize from a clean .2-second RTT, double the timeout, ignore an ambiguous
.8-second ACK, then accept a new clean .2-second sample. The diagram reads each
committed event's actual RTO and action. Its arrows represent estimator events,
not packet transmissions or elapsed network time.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karn_events.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::KarnEstimator k;
    const std::vector<dm::algorithms::KarnEvent> events = {k.ack(.2),
                                                           k.timeout(),
                                                           k.ack(.8, true),
                                                           k.ack(.2)};
    const char *names[] = {"ignored", "first", "clean", "timeout"};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    std::print("| event | action | SRTT before | RTO before | SRTT after | RTO after |\n| ---: | --- | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < events.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = events[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", i,
                   names[int(e.action)], e.before.srtt, e.before.rto,
                   e.after.srtt, e.after.rto);
        d.node(std::to_string(i), {5. * i, 0},
               std::format("{}\nactual RTO {:.3f}s", names[int(e.action)],
                           e.after.rto));
        if (i)
            d.edge(std::to_string(i - 1), std::to_string(i));
    }
    d.save_svg("build/karn_events.svg");
}
```
