| 1 | timeout | 0.200000000 | 0.600000000 | 0.200000000 | 1.200000000 |
| 2 | ignored | 0.200000000 | 1.200000000 | 0.200000000 | 1.200000000 |
| 3 | clean | 0.200000000 | 1.200000000 | 0.200000000 | 0.500000000 |
\image(figures/karn_events.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual clean, timeout, ignored and recovery transitions.)
\alttext(The timeout doubles RTO, the ambiguous ACK leaves it unchanged, and a fresh clean sample recomputes it.)

> Separate measurement ambiguity from smoothing

The first clean sample R initializes mean R and deviation R/2. Later clean
updates use the old mean in the deviation calculation:

$$
V'=\tfrac34 V+\tfrac14|S-R|,\quad S'=\tfrac78 S+\tfrac18 R,\quad RTO'=S'+4V'.
$$
\alttext(The deviation uses the old smoothed RTT before the smoothed RTT itself is updated; the educational timeout is new mean plus four new deviations.)

An ignored ACK changes no field. A timeout doubles current RTO without updating
SRTT or RTTVAR. A subsequent clean sample recomputes RTO and can reduce
accumulated backoff. Retransmitted samples are discarded before validation
because their numeric RTT is unused.

This is an educational transition model. It omits clock granularity, a
minimum/maximum RTO, timestamp disambiguation, packet sequence state and actual
timer management. A value below one second here is therefore not evidence that
the implementation is a complete RFC6298 TCP timer. Samples and all state values
use seconds; horizontal event indices below are not seconds.

> Keep the original nine events

The original sequence contains four clean samples around .2 seconds, an ignored
retransmitted ACK of .8, a timeout, and three clean recovery samples. We retain
that exact order as a synthetic estimator experiment without asserting a
packet-level causal chronology.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karn_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::KarnEstimator k(1);
    struct Input {
        double sample;
        bool retransmitted;
        bool timeout;
    };
    const std::vector<Input> inputs = {{.20, false, false}, {.22, false, false},
                                       {.19, false, false}, {.21, false, false},
                                       {.80, true, false}, {0, false, true},
                                       {.23, false, false}, {.20, false, false},
                                       {.21, false, false}};
    std::vector<double> x, mean, rto;
    std::print("| event | action | RTT sample | SRTT | RTTVAR | actual RTO |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    const char *names[] = {"ignored", "first", "clean", "timeout"};
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &s = inputs[i];
        const auto e =
            s.timeout ? k.timeout() : k.ack(s.sample, s.retransmitted);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n", i,
                   names[int(e.action)], e.sample, e.after.srtt, e.after.rttvar,
                   e.after.rto);
        x.push_back(i);
        mean.push_back(e.after.srtt);
        rto.push_back(e.after.rto);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, mean, "SRTT", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, mean, "", {37, 99, 235},
                                                     4).line(x, rto, "RTO",
                                                             {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, rto, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4).title("Original estimator events and clean recovery").x_label("event ordinal, not elapsed seconds").y_label("seconds").y_limits(0, 1.5).save_svg("build/karn_original.svg");
}
```
