> Check the constant-input recurrence

For repeated clean .2-second RTT samples after first initialization, the mean
remains .2. The initial deviation .1 is multiplied by .75 on every later sample.
The known recurrence .1 times .75 to the power i is a control for update order;
the program plots actual states and checks the relation within floating
tolerance. There is no arbitrary one-second clamp hiding the estimator's
asymptote in this teaching model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karn_profile.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::KarnEstimator k;
    std::vector<double> x, y, v;
    std::print("| clean sample ordinal | actual SRTT | actual RTTVAR | actual RTO |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < 40; ++i) {
        const auto e = k.ack(.2);
        if (std::fabs(e.after.rttvar - .1 * std::pow(.75, i)) > 1e-15)
            throw std::runtime_error("constant input recurrence");
        if (i < 4 || i == 9 || i == 19 || i == 39)
            std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12e} | {:.12f} |\n", i,
                       e.after.srtt, e.after.rttvar, e.after.rto);
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(e.after.rto);
        v.push_back(e.after.rttvar);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "RTO", {220, 38, 38}, 2).line(x, v, "RTTVAR", {37, 99, 235}, 2).title("Actual constant-input decay without protocol clamps").x_label("clean sample ordinal").y_label("seconds").y_limits(-.02, .8).save_svg("build/karn_profile.svg");
}
```
